{"task":"anchor: Open question: switch this machine from persite to auto mode","goals":"Get sites.ldev falling back to the projects dashboard, and get the bare-directory naming fix live on this machine","status":"Questions","recorded_at":"2026-09-09T12:23:56Z","body":"The bare-directory change (a015819) lands in the auto-mode Caddyfile template only. This machine is MODE=persite, where nothing binds 80/443 and there is no wildcard block, so neither the dashboard fallback nor bare directory names take effect until the mode changes. Switching means a root launchd daemon on 80/443, and stopping the running seasonal-drops Caddy first because it holds admin port 2019 that auto mode also wants. Needs Bryce's decision.","parent_commit":"a015819fbf0ca6d34d321b513d727f9c54f42898","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"60","tasks":[{"id":"diagnose","content":"Diagnose sites.ldev: persite mode, nothing on 80/443, no wildcard fallback","status":"completed"},{"id":"bare-dirs","content":"Serve bare directory names in the auto template, verified against real ~/Sites","status":"completed"},{"id":"list","content":"Make ldev list report bare dirs and flag unreachable names","status":"completed"},{"id":"mode","content":"Decide how to change this machine so the fallback actually works","status":"pending"},{"id":"docs","content":"Document bare directory names in the auto-mode docs (README held by a peer session)","status":"pending"}],"questions":[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Persite mode — drop it as an install-wide mode? The four capabilities docs/persite.md justifies it with survive either way as a per-site escalation. What is genuinely at stake is that persite is the only way to run ldev with no root and nothing on ports 80/443.","kind":"decision","required":true,"description":null,"priority":null,"source":null,"original_ask":null,"provenance":{"at":"2026-09-09T12:23:56Z","session":{"id":"3e8f56a2-7837-42a5-adfb-4e072f3876ee","provider":"claude","title":"https://sites.ldev/ (or any other name I pu